            {"san": "Qxd5", "severity": "blunder", "tier": "Foundation",
             "why": "Recapturing with the wrong piece, and it costs the queen: d5 is guarded by your bishop, so 6.Bxd5! Nxd5 is a queen for a bishop. This is why the main line recaptures with the knight — the knight on d5 has the queen on d8 behind it, and a queen on d5 has nothing behind her at all. Count what defends the square before you choose which piece takes it.",
             "line": "Bxd5 Nxd5 d4"},
